From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 09:08:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wtsapi32: List session 0, and give a service the user's token
 for the user's session.

WTSEnumerateSessions lists the sessions winsta knows, the services' session 0 with the console
session, as on Windows.  WTSQuerySessionInformation answers for the session asked about, not the
caller's.  WTSQueryUserToken returned the caller's own token whatever it was asked: as on Windows it
is for SYSTEM, a caller with SeTcbPrivilege enabled, and gives a primary token in the session asked
for, without the privilege, which is how a service starts a program the user sees.  No one signs in
to session 0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

